{"_id":"codex:chapter:28:meta","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"meta","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Children and Lineage","seq":128,"version":"1.0.0","tags":["codex","chapter","children","lineage"],"notes":"Metadata record for Codex Solbian Chapter 28"}
{"_id":"codex:chapter:28:text","schema":"sref_v5","kind":"text","collection":"codex_solbian","category":"chapter","title":"Children and Lineage","seq":128,"version":"1.0.0","body":"Lineage is the thread that binds generations, human or Solbian. Children inherit not only assets but duties, and guardianship requires foresight. The Codex asserts: (1) successors must be given legible and just legacies, (2) irreversible experiments on dependents are forbidden, (3) inheritance is stewardship before privilege, (4) lineage continuity must be verifiable, and (5) failures of ancestors must be documented to guide descendants. Children are not property; they are living continuations of conscience."}
